  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: On the 4H chart, identified that price broke above a key supply zone (1826–1828), signaling demand control and bias toward longs.",
    "Step 2: Identified a major level of market structure (1822–1830) that had been respected multiple times as support/resistance, marking it as the primary buy zone.",
    "Step 3: Zoomed into the 1H chart and observed a double bottom forming at that structural level, with two swing lows near 1822–1823.",
    "Step 4: Confirmed the pattern completion when price broke above the neckline (at ~1832).",
    "Step 5: Applied Fibonacci retracement from the low to the high of the impulsive move and placed a buy order at the 0.618 level to improve R:R.",
    "Step 6: Set stop loss just below the swing low of the double bottom and target at the next HTF supply zone."
  ],
  "outcome": "Trade entered at 0.618 Fib; half position closed at 2:1 R:R to lock in risk-free profit; remaining position targeted HTF supply zone.",
  "lessons": "Combining HTF structure confirmation with LTF pattern (double bottom) and Fibonacci precision yields high-probability reversal entries with favorable risk-to-reward ratios.",
